      "text": "CTI context (Microsoft Threat Intelligence): Microsoft Threat Intelligence reports distributed password spraying with few attempts per account across many accounts, including low-volume patterns. This is external campaign context. PurpleSharp's short multi-account failure burst can be compared with that pattern, without transferring actor identity, compromised credentials or campaign IOC conclusions to local hosts. Publisher-reported technical context; does not establish behavior, compromise or C2 purpose in Mordor hosts.",
